WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:08.322
PROFESSOR: So in Mesoamerican
cosmology and its creation stories,

00:00:08.322 --> 00:00:09.530
which-- there are many types.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:15.170
There is one theme that really helps
us understand divination and prediction

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:18.590
practices among the
Aztecs and then the Maya.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:21.140
And the story goes
that, in the beginning,

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.837
as in many paradisiacal stories--

00:00:23.837 --> 00:00:25.670
in the beginning, there
was a period of time

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:32.229
where heaven and earth were close
together, where the beings who existed

00:00:32.229 --> 00:00:38.510
could speak to animals, where
divinities and humans were almost

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:40.100
on the same plane.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.220
Our ancestors and divinities
were close, and they all

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:48.080
had the same powers of
seeing, of observing.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:53.900
But in the Mesoamerican case,
what happens is, the deities--

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.870
for some reason, they become
jealous that the ancestors,

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:01.580
who are closer to humans,
who've not yet been created,

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.720
have the same powers that they have.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:07.970
And then they decide that
they don't like this.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:12.110
And so they create a separation.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:19.460
And the way they create the separation
is, they cast a spell over the vision--

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:24.560
over the eyes of the
ancestors, which is described

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.660
as though a breath on a mirror.

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:30.950
And there's still a mirror, but when
the ancestors-- and, eventually,

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:35.900
the humans-- look into the
mirror, they can't see as clearly.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.780
They can't see as far into the mirror.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:40.310
They can't see themselves.

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:42.230
They can't see the world.

00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:45.450
And, therefore, what happens is
that, when human beings are created,

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:49.340
they inherit this breath over
the mirror, over their eyes.

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:53.030
And they can still see the
world that all of us see.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:56.830
But, in fact, the world is
so much more full of life.

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:59.400
It's all around-- that we can't see.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.340
And, therefore, the divinities can see.

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.230
They can see inside of trees.

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:05.640
They can see inside of our bodies.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.640
They can see through mountains.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.590
They can see great distances--

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:12.390
all things that we cannot do.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:19.010
And so what happens is that
certain individuals in the society

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:25.520
are born who have a little
bit more capacity for vision,

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.680
and those often become the diviners.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.710
They have to undergo
training, special training,

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:34.040
to take this extra ability
to see that moves them

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:37.370
a little closer to the
ancestors or to the divinities.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:41.210
And they take this training-- what
we might call shamanistic training--

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:44.240
to sharpen this ability.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:48.020
And they're often the ones who can read
the signs, who become the diviners.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:52.340
But this idea of the mirror is very
important in Mexico and Mesoamerica

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:54.650
because many of these
mirrors were made out

00:02:54.650 --> 00:03:00.290
of obsidian, this black obsidian stone
that was very brittle and very sharp,

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:01.720
but it could be shined.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:02.530
You could shine it.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.250
And when you looked into it--
and I've looked into them--

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.470
you can see yourself.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:09.110
Now, you can't see themself as clearly
as when we look into our mirrors,

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:12.470
but you can see yourself.

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:15.090
And sometimes, you can
see things behind you.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:20.510
And so these mirrors become very
important for humans as techniques

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.940
to improve their own ability to see.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:29.440
By having these mirrors, it improves,
clarifies that breath on the eyes.

